# Scoped to hydra/ like .clang-format; pinned to clang-tidy 22.1.8 (the
# clang-format wheel's twin — `pip install --user clang-tidy==22.1.8`).
# Runs over the full tree's compile database; the ritual command lives in
# README.md. Warnings are errors so the ritual is a gate, and every check
# family below is curated — additions welcome, silent removals not.
#
# The opt-outs:
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: everything geometric here takes
#   adjacent same-typed floats and dimensions; the signal drowns.
# - bugprone-reserved-identifier: the delegate is written in USD's house
#   style, and `_CapitalizedInternal` is that style's private-name
#   convention (technically reserved, universally used across pxr).
# - performance-enum-size: the wire enums mirror cenote-wire's Rust
#   spellings and are never stored in bulk; shrinking them buys nothing.
# - deprecated-declarations (via ExtraArgs — a compiler diagnostic, not a
#   check): USD's TfType::Define probes std::is_pod_v, which libstdc++ 15
#   deprecates, and clang surfaces the system-header diagnostic because
#   the template instantiates from our registrations. USD's noise, not
#   ours — real deprecations in our own code stay fatal in the -Werror
#   compile.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  readability-const-return-type,
  readability-container-size-empty,
  readability-delete-null-pointer,
  readability-duplicate-include,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-redundant-smartptr-get,
  readability-redundant-string-cstr,
  readability-static-definition-in-anonymous-namespace
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: 'hydra/(hdCenote|transport|wire)/'
ExtraArgs: ['-Wno-deprecated-declarations']
